# Scope inputs read by the OCaml runtime's `Value.from_json`

`main.ml` reads each `input*.json` with `Value.from_json` on the input
structure generated by the OCaml backend; the results must be those of the
interpreter on the same input.

> Module From_json_e2e

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration Status:
  -- Single
  -- Married content date
  -- Other content (integer, money)

declaration structure Stay:
  data arrival content date
  data length content duration

declaration scope S:
  input id content integer
  input rate content decimal
  input income content money
  input resident content boolean
  input status content Status
  input stays content list of Stay
  input spouse_income content optional of money
  context bonus content money
  output echo content (integer, decimal, money, boolean, Status)
  output stays_out content list of Stay
  output spouse_out content optional of money
  output bonus_out content money
  output literal content Stay
```

```catala
scope S:
  definition bonus equals $0
  definition echo equals (id, rate, income, resident, status)
  definition stays_out equals stays
  definition spouse_out equals spouse_income
  definition bonus_out equals bonus
  definition literal equals
    #[json = "{\"arrival\": {\"year\": 2020, \"month\": 2, \"day\": 29}, \"length\": {\"days\": 3}}"]
    Stay
```
